13:T5ad,Wearing protective gloves and earplugs, a worker feeds lengths of wood into a machine that makes an earsplitting whine as it automatically cuts a groove into the end of each piece.  Nearby, stacks of wooden wedges wait to be slotted into those grooves to form the beginnings of a hockey stick.  Further down the Roustan Hockey production line, other workers are busy shaping, trimming, sanding, painting and screen printing as they turn lumber into a Canadian national symbol.  It’s a typical day on the job for the 15 workers at Canada’s last major hockey stick factory, 60 miles (100 kilometers) southwest of Toronto.  The operation has origins that date back to the 1800s and has survived decades of trade globalization to hang on as the last North American commercial manufacturer of traditional wooden hockey sticks.  Now it’s facing fresh headwinds from the trade war launched by U. S.  President Donald Trump, who has ripped up free trade deals in North America and imposed tariffs on Canadian exports.  The uncertainty is making life a headache for Roustan.  “You never know” what Trump will do, said Bo Crawford, the factory’s general manager.  “You just have to roll with it and the president of the U. S.  can change his mind day to day, week to week, hour to hour.  So yeah, we have to deal with it the best we can,” he said.  Roustan has spent months dealing with U. S.  customer worries and navigating the trade challenges.4:[["$","$Lf",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"NewsArticle\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://www.pressorahub.com/business/roustan-hockey-canada-tariffs/\"},\"headline\":\"Canada’s last hockey stick factory survives in face of tariff threats and globalization\",\"description\":\"Roustan Hockey, Canada’s last major wooden hockey stick manufacturer, faces challenges from U.S. tariffs and shifting global production. The artisanal factory continues producing traditional sticks amid declining demand, preserving both Canadian craftsmanship and a national sports legacy.\",\"image\":\"/images/roustan-hockey-factory.webp\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"David Miller\",\"url\":\"https://www.pressorahub.com/our-team/\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"PressoraHub\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://www.pressorahub.com/images/pressorahub-icon.webp\"}},\"datePublished\":\"2025-06-18T00:00:00.000Z\",\"dateModified\":\"2025-06-18T00:00:00.000Z\"}"}}],["$","$L10",null,{"breadcrumbTitle":"Canada’s last hockey stick factory survives in face of tariff threats and globalization","category":"business","children":["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"post-layout-1 padding","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"top-content","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"post-card single-card","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"post-content","children":[["$","$L11",null,{"title":"roustan-hockey-canada-tariffs","href":"/business","className":"card-btn bg-green","children":"business"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"title","style":{"lineHeight":1.3},"children":"Canada’s last hockey stick factory survives in face of tariff threats and globalization"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"post-list","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"author","children":["by ",["$","span",null,{"children":"David Miller"}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"date","children":"October 6, 2025"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Roustan Hockey, Canada’s last major wooden hockey stick manufacturer, faces challenges from U.S. tariffs and shifting global production. The artisanal factory continues producing traditional sticks amid declining demand, preserving both Canadian craftsmanship and a national sports legacy."}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"post-social","children":["$","ul",null,{"className":"social-list d-flex align-items-center","children":[["$","li",null,{}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L11",null,{"href":"https://www.instagram.com/millerdavid4569/","className":"instagram","children":["$","i",null,{"className":"lab la-instagram"}]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L11",null,{"href":"https://medium.com/@david_miller_48409","className":"","style":{"border":""},"children":["$","i",null,{"className":"lab la-medium"}]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L11",null,{"href":"https://substack.com/@davidmiller170279","className":"pinterest","children":["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"20","height":"15","viewBox":"0 0 256 256","children":["$","g",null,{"transform":"scale(5.12,5.12)","children":[["$","path",null,{"d":"M43,11h-35v-6h35z"}],["$","path",null,{"d":"M43,19h-35v-6h35z"}],["$","path",null,{"d":"M43,44.805l-17.016,-10.636l-17.984,10.579v-23.748h35z"}]]}]}]}]}]]}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"row","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"col-lg-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"post-layout-content","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"layout-thumb mb-30","children":["$","$L12",null,{"title":"Canada’s last hockey stick factory survives in face of tariff threats and globalization","src":"/images/roustan-hockey-factory.webp","alt":"Canada’s last hockey stick factory survives in face of tariff threats and globalization","width":1200,"height":800,"priority":true,"style":{"width":"100%","height":"auto"}}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"layout-desc","style":{"marginBottom":"1rem"},"children":"$13"}],"$L14","$L15","$L16"]}],"$L17","$L18"]}]}],"$L19"]}]]}]}],"$L1a"]}]}]]
